# Aetherfield gateway application options.
#
# GW_INDEX is a Kconfig symbol rather than a bare #define so it can be set from
# a .conf fragment per build configuration. That matters when flashing several
# gateways in a row: editing a header between builds is how two gateways end up
# both claiming 10.10.0.11, which works perfectly until all of them are live.

menu "Aetherfield gateway"

config GW_INDEX
	int "Gateway index within this server's group (1..30)"
	default 1
	range 1 30
	help
	  Sets three things at once, all of which must be unique per gateway:
	    the HELLO name     gw-01 .. gw-30
	    the static IP      10.10.0.11 .. 10.10.0.40
	    the TCP source port 50001 .. 50030

	  It ALSO sets this gateway's slot in the downlink stagger, so at 30
	  gateways they do not all transmit the same command on the same
	  millisecond. See GW_CMD_STAGGER_MS in gw_config.h.

	  Pick it with an extra Kconfig fragment (gw01.conf, gw02.conf, ...)
	  rather than by editing a file, so every gateway builds from identical
	  source.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
